Dirk Zimmermann wrote:
>
>> > Now my biggest early obstacle/weakness right now seems to be armor. I
>> > tend to avoid upgrading my studded leather armor because it disturbs
>> > my casting, and without my spells I'm just a very weak fighter even
>> > with reasonable dagger skill.
>
> I think it's pretty much leather/dragonskin/fabric only, and that's
> for body armor too. That means mithril coats from the mines are out of
> question too if I want to cast a lot.

In vanilla Nethack this teaches conservative exploration strategy for
early wizards.  Do you wear the first mithril you can confirm to be not
cursed and play with missiles and pets, or do you go with very poor AC
and try to build up spell school skills early?  Sometimes the first
studded leather armor comes from the pet killing watchmen on the way
back up from mines end and that's a lot of early game experience later
than the first mithril.

Learning to survive as a weak fighter makes playing strong fighter
classes more ascendable.


